course: dictionary
lesson: 6725
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word oil is a good example. «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air» means oil is a fuel from under the ground, not a cooking liquid.
explain: Look at the words around oil. In «A family in Ohio left a pan of oil on the hob», the hob and the pan tell you it is cooking oil. In «Oil the squeaky gate», oil is a verb, a doing word, meaning to put oil on something.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense. If «oil» means cooking liquid and the sentence is about a machine, the swap will not fit, so try another meaning.
fact: Oil is a thick, slippery liquid that does not mix with water.
fact: Oil floats on water because it is less dense.
fact: Crude oil from under the ground is made into petrol, diesel and plastic.
fact: As a verb, «oil» means to put oil on something, such as a machine or a squeaky hinge.
fact: Never put water on an oil fire: turn off the heat and cover the pan.
exercise: «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air.» What kind of oil is meant here? | Oil for slippery machine parts | Olive oil for cooking | *Fuel from under the ground, like crude oil | Oil paint for pictures
exercise: «Please oil the bike chain so it stops squeaking.» What does oil mean here? | A kind of oil paint | *To put oil on something | A thick black liquid from under the ground | A cooking liquid for frying
exercise: A family in Ohio left a pan of oil on the hob, and it caught fire. What should they have done instead of throwing water on it? | *Turn off the heat and cover the pan | Pour in more oil | Throw more water on it | Leave the kitchen and open the back door wide
test: Why does oil float on water? | Because it dissolves in water | Because it is heavier than water | *Because it is less dense than water | Because it is made from plants only
test: Sam reads «an oil rig in the sea». What is an oil rig? | *A structure that drills for oil under the sea | A kind of paintbrush | A boat for catching fish | A pan for frying eggs
exam: «Oil and water don't mix.» What does this tell you about oil? | It is a gas that floats away | *It does not mix with water | It is always black | It mixes easily with water
